//! TypeScript contract generation (feature `ts`). `generate()` returns the whole text of
//! `web/src/contract/generated.ts`; `examples/contract_ts.rs` writes it and
//! `tests/contract_ts.rs` fails when the committed file is stale.
//! Only wire types derive `TS` (never `sim-types`), so money is dollars (`f64` -> `number`).
//! The type list below is checked: a test fails when a type reaches the wire without being listed.
use ts_rs::{Config, TS};

